<title>CROATIA: Croatia, Siemens sign DM 152 mln rail deal.</title>
<headline>Croatia, Siemens sign DM 152 mln rail deal.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia's state-owned railway company Hrvatske Zeljeznice on Thursday signed a 152 million German marks deal to buy 30 passenger carriages from Siemens AG Austria and have 40 others repaired and upgraded.</p>
<p>According to the national news agency HINA, first deliveries are planned for September next year. The whole deal is to be completed by the end of 1988.</p>
<p>With this new purchase Hrvatske Zeljeznice plans to upgrade the level of its international services, HINA quoted director Marijan Klaric as saying.</p>
<p>-- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
